# Implementation Planning — {{project_name}}

This skill specializes the Coder Nexus `implementation-planning` process for **{{project_name}}**: phases remain vertical behavior slices, `PHASE-00` runs first, a single `code_writer` executes tasks in order, and `validate_plan_slices` must report `PASS`.

---

## 1. Non-Negotiable Planning Rules (`IP1`–`IP17`)

- **Vertical Behavior Slices & Layer Order (`IP1`, `IP13`)**: Every phase delivers one testable behavior ordered as `{{order_summary}}`. After `PHASE-00`, schedule the highest-risk vertical behavior first (`IP9`, `IP13`).
- **Plan Header Sections (`IP10`, `IP11`)**: Place `## Global constraints` (verbatim spec values with `BR-NN` / `D-NN` IDs) and `## Review focus` (up to 5 uncovered inputs/failure modes mapped to owning tasks, or `None found after checking every AC and BR`) above `## AC coverage` in `implementation-plan.md`. Missing spec values or expected results become `Q-NN` before Gate 3.
- **Prefactor & Wide Renames (`IP14`, `IP15`)**: Schedule behavior-preserving prefactors as the first task of a phase (`PASS` on existing tests). Execute wide renames as **expand → migrate (bounded batches) → contract** keeping every task check `PASS`.
- **Single-Writer Task Shape & Sizing (`IP2`–`IP4`, `IP12`, `IP16`)**: One task = architecture-aligned file scope (`clean-architecture`) + exact signatures and pinned constants (never transcribed function bodies) + one targeted check command with `cwd`. Split any task that is `XL`, touches 8+ files, has `"and"` in its title, or crosses two subsystems.
- **Tests & Docs Inside Every Phase (`IP17`)**: Unit/integration tests and doc updates belong inside the phase whose behavior they verify; never create a standalone final testing, docs, or polish phase.
- **Parent-Ticket Branch & Verified Commit Checkpoints (`IP7`, `G2`, `G3`, `M3`, `M10`)**: Work branches use the parent/umbrella ticket (`<type>/<PARENT-TICKET>-<short-description>`, or `<type>/<short-description>` when no ticket exists). Every phase or sub-ticket boundary maps to an explicit verified commit checkpoint (`<type>(<SUB-TICKET>): <summary> [parent: <PARENT-TICKET>, PHASE-NN]`, `<type>(<PARENT-TICKET>): [PHASE-NN] <summary>`, or `<type>(phase-NN): <summary>`) — never arbitrary WIP commits. Production merges (`main`) and tags are user-only commands (`M6`).
- **Out-of-Workspace Handoffs (`IP8`)**: Changes outside this workspace are recorded as `PHASE-00` handoffs or `BLOCKED`, never `code_writer` tasks.

